1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,814
In nineteen eighteen, a magazine for baby
stores gave parents a simple rule:

2
00:00:04,814 --> 00:00:06,297
pink is for boys.

3
00:00:06,297 --> 00:00:08,050
Blue is for girls.

4
00:00:08,050 --> 00:00:11,176
It wasn't a joke, and it wasn't a mistake.

5
00:00:11,176 --> 00:00:15,678
It was the advice of the day, printed for
the people who sold baby clothes.

6
00:00:15,678 --> 00:00:20,835
So how did the color for boys become the
color for girls in just a few decades?

7
00:00:20,835 --> 00:00:23,954
And who decided that a newborn needs a
color at all?

8
00:00:24,554 --> 00:00:26,592
The Color You Were Told to Wear.

9
00:00:27,192 --> 00:00:30,588
Go back to the eighteen hundreds and look
at a family photo.

10
00:00:30,588 --> 00:00:33,397
Every small child is in a white dress.

11
00:00:33,397 --> 00:00:34,353
The girls, yes.

12
00:00:34,353 --> 00:00:35,141
The boys too.

13
00:00:35,141 --> 00:00:42,453
There's a famous photo of a two year old
Franklin Roosevelt in a white dress, long
hair, and a feathered hat,

14
00:00:42,453 --> 00:00:45,127
and in his time nobody would have blinked.

15
00:00:45,127 --> 00:00:46,785
White was practical.

16
00:00:46,785 --> 00:00:48,003
Babies are messy,

17
00:00:48,003 --> 00:00:51,846
and white cotton could be boiled and
bleached until it looked new again.

18
00:00:51,846 --> 00:00:55,920
A dress was easy to change, easy to let
out as the child grew,

19
00:00:55,920 --> 00:01:00,541
and easy to pass down from one child to
the next, no matter who came next.

20
00:01:00,541 --> 00:01:04,166
Boys only got their first trousers at
around six or seven.

21
00:01:04,166 --> 00:01:08,667
It was a big day, almost a ceremony, with
a haircut and a new suit.

22
00:01:08,667 --> 00:01:11,693
Until then, a baby was just a baby.

23
00:01:11,693 --> 00:01:16,481
Pastel colors did show up in the middle of
the century, pink and blue among them.

24
00:01:16,481 --> 00:01:18,935
But they were decoration, not a rule.

25
00:01:18,935 --> 00:01:22,101
A little pink ribbon said nothing about
who was wearing it.

26
00:01:22,701 --> 00:01:30,510
Then, in June nineteen eighteen, a trade
magazine called Infant's Department told
store owners what the accepted rule was.

27
00:01:30,510 --> 00:01:32,869
Pink for the boy, blue for the girl.

28
00:01:32,869 --> 00:01:34,546
And it gave a reason.

29
00:01:34,546 --> 00:01:39,803
Pink, it said, is a more decided and
stronger color, so it suits a boy.

30
00:01:39,803 --> 00:01:44,132
Blue is more delicate and dainty, so it's
prettier for a girl.

31
00:01:44,132 --> 00:01:45,467
Think about that.

32
00:01:45,467 --> 00:01:52,226
The same logic people use today, strong
versus delicate, was used to argue the
exact opposite.

33
00:01:52,226 --> 00:01:57,636
Pink was seen as a lighter shade of red,
the color of soldiers' coats and fighting
spirit.

34
00:01:57,636 --> 00:02:02,431
Blue, some said, was the color of calm and
of the Virgin Mary.

35
00:02:02,431 --> 00:02:04,655
The colors didn't carry meaning.

36
00:02:04,655 --> 00:02:07,867
The meaning was attached to them, by
whoever was selling.

37
00:02:08,467 --> 00:02:10,520
And sellers did not agree.

38
00:02:10,520 --> 00:02:17,503
In nineteen twenty seven, Time magazine
asked the biggest department stores in
America which color was for which child.

39
00:02:17,503 --> 00:02:20,276
Filene's in Boston said pink for boys.

40
00:02:20,276 --> 00:02:25,895
So did Marshall Field's in Chicago, Best
and Company in New York, and Halle
Brothers in Cleveland.

41
00:02:25,895 --> 00:02:27,919
Other stores said the opposite.

42
00:02:27,919 --> 00:02:31,374
Imagine being a new parent in nineteen
twenty seven.

43
00:02:31,374 --> 00:02:34,004
You buy a pink outfit for your son in
Chicago,

44
00:02:34,004 --> 00:02:36,005
visit your sister in another city,

45
00:02:36,005 --> 00:02:38,899
and her local store tells you that you got
it backwards.

46
00:02:38,899 --> 00:02:42,778
Historians still argue about how common
each version was.

47
00:02:42,778 --> 00:02:47,981
One study of old newspapers found both
versions printed side by side for decades.

48
00:02:47,981 --> 00:02:50,950
The honest answer is that there was no
rule.

49
00:02:50,950 --> 00:02:53,868
There were stores, and each store had a
guess.

50
00:02:54,468 --> 00:02:58,000
Somewhere in the middle of the twentieth
century, the guesses settled.

51
00:02:58,000 --> 00:02:59,657
Pink went to girls.

52
00:02:59,657 --> 00:03:01,457
Blue went to boys.

53
00:03:01,457 --> 00:03:03,041
No law was passed.

54
00:03:03,041 --> 00:03:05,032
No scientist proved anything.

55
00:03:05,032 --> 00:03:10,613
Manufacturers and stores simply kept
repeating the same pairing until it felt
like nature.

56
00:03:10,613 --> 00:03:15,351
In the nineteen fifties, pink became the
color of grown up femininity too.

57
00:03:15,351 --> 00:03:20,446
When Mamie Eisenhower wore a pink gown to
her husband's inauguration in nineteen
fifty three,

58
00:03:20,446 --> 00:03:22,011
the press loved it,

59
00:03:22,011 --> 00:03:27,708
and soon there were pink kitchens, pink
bathrooms, and pink appliances in American
homes.

60
00:03:27,708 --> 00:03:31,610
The baby boom generation grew up color
coded from the crib.

61
00:03:31,610 --> 00:03:33,824
Boys in blue, girls in pink,

62
00:03:33,824 --> 00:03:36,917
and every relative knew exactly what gift
to bring.

63
00:03:37,517 --> 00:03:39,748
Then something strange happened.

64
00:03:39,748 --> 00:03:43,651
In the late sixties and seventies, many
parents rejected it.

65
00:03:43,651 --> 00:03:48,648
The women's movement pushed back against
the idea that girls had to look soft and
sweet.

66
00:03:48,648 --> 00:03:50,577
Unisex clothes took over.

67
00:03:50,577 --> 00:03:54,462
Overalls, stripes, red, yellow, green.

68
00:03:54,462 --> 00:04:01,442
Reportedly, for two whole years in the
seventies, the Sears catalog didn't show a
single pink toddler outfit.

69
00:04:01,442 --> 00:04:04,290
For a moment, it looked like the rule was
dying,

70
00:04:04,290 --> 00:04:07,244
and that kids might go back to being just
kids.

71
00:04:07,844 --> 00:04:09,363
It wasn't dying.

72
00:04:09,363 --> 00:04:12,699
In the nineteen eighties, prenatal tests
became common,

73
00:04:12,699 --> 00:04:17,101
and parents could learn whether it was a
boy or a girl months before the birth.

74
00:04:17,101 --> 00:04:19,438
That gave stores something new to sell:

75
00:04:19,438 --> 00:04:20,479
time.

76
00:04:20,479 --> 00:04:24,587
Now you could shop for a specific kind of
baby before it arrived.

77
00:04:24,587 --> 00:04:26,503
And the industry noticed.

78
00:04:26,503 --> 00:04:28,819
Neutral clothes started to disappear.

79
00:04:28,819 --> 00:04:32,142
A plain blue romper suddenly had a little
football on it.

80
00:04:32,142 --> 00:04:34,819
A plain pink one got a bow and a kitten.

81
00:04:34,819 --> 00:04:37,442
And pink spread far beyond clothes.

82
00:04:37,442 --> 00:04:39,513
Strollers. Car seats.

83
00:04:39,513 --> 00:04:41,980
Bottles. Bedding. Wallpaper.

84
00:04:41,980 --> 00:04:45,428
Historian Jo Paoletti put the logic in one
line.

85
00:04:45,428 --> 00:04:48,830
The more you individualize clothing, the
more you can sell.

86
00:04:49,430 --> 00:04:53,851
By the two thousands, the split covered
almost everything a child could touch.

87
00:04:53,851 --> 00:04:56,972
Toy stores had a pink aisle and a blue
aisle.

88
00:04:56,972 --> 00:05:00,085
Building bricks got a separate pink line
for girls.

89
00:05:00,085 --> 00:05:02,292
And it didn't stop at childhood.

90
00:05:02,292 --> 00:05:09,165
In twenty fifteen, a New York City study
compared nearly eight hundred products
sold in a men's and a women's version.

91
00:05:09,165 --> 00:05:13,112
On average, the women's version cost about
seven percent more,

92
00:05:13,112 --> 00:05:15,941
often for the same item in a different
color.

93
00:05:15,941 --> 00:05:18,712
People started calling it the pink tax.

94
00:05:18,712 --> 00:05:25,207
Then, in two thousand eight, an American
mother cut into a cake at a party to
reveal pink frosting inside,

95
00:05:25,207 --> 00:05:26,934
and posted about it online.

96
00:05:26,934 --> 00:05:29,340
The gender reveal party was born.

97
00:05:29,340 --> 00:05:34,030
Today it's a whole industry of balloons,
smoke cannons and confetti,

98
00:05:34,030 --> 00:05:37,704
all built on one question: pink or blue?

99
00:05:38,304 --> 00:05:40,231
Here's the quiet genius of it.

100
00:05:40,231 --> 00:05:43,858
A white dress could go from a big sister
to a little brother.

101
00:05:43,858 --> 00:05:45,666
A pink stroller can't.

102
00:05:45,666 --> 00:05:47,258
Not easily, anyway.

103
00:05:47,258 --> 00:05:52,203
Most parents feel a small pinch of
awkwardness pushing their son in something
bright pink,

104
00:05:52,203 --> 00:05:54,563
and that small pinch is enough.

105
00:05:54,563 --> 00:05:59,011
A second child of the other sex now means
a second set of everything.

106
00:05:59,011 --> 00:06:01,263
Nobody ever told you to buy twice.

107
00:06:01,263 --> 00:06:05,158
They just painted the first set a color
that made reusing it feel wrong.

108
00:06:05,158 --> 00:06:07,212
And the rule teaches itself.

109
00:06:07,212 --> 00:06:10,967
Kids learn it from the aisles, from the
gifts, from the cake.

110
00:06:10,967 --> 00:06:14,180
By the age of four, many of them will
police it for you.

111
00:06:14,180 --> 00:06:18,807
Every time a store builds a pink aisle and
a blue aisle, the rule gets taught again,

112
00:06:18,807 --> 00:06:21,694
to a new set of parents who think they're
choosing freely.

113
00:06:22,294 --> 00:06:27,424
A hundred years ago, a magazine told
parents that pink was strong enough for a
boy.

114
00:06:27,424 --> 00:06:31,357
Today, the same color is supposed to be
too soft for him.

115
00:06:31,357 --> 00:06:33,151
The color never changed.

116
00:06:33,151 --> 00:06:35,177
Only the story around it did.

117
00:06:35,177 --> 00:06:38,852
So the next time someone asks, is it a boy
or a girl,

118
00:06:38,852 --> 00:06:41,298
notice what the question really means:

119
00:06:41,298 --> 00:06:43,331
which aisle are we shopping in?

120
00:06:43,331 --> 00:06:44,811
Made to Want.
